From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:01:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The retired reflection rungs leave the shader

Patch 0023 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The reflections were removed on 2026-09-30 and their six candidate rungs came off the Experiment
row, but the tests that implemented them stayed in the shader and in the classification. That
would only be dead code, except that the shade rungs of patch 0022 were given the numbers 31 to
33, and candidates A (31) and C (33) live in radianceFrom, which the BOUNCE pass calls as well as
the reflection pass. So "Shade: local after knee" also took the bounce's light from the frame
times the direct light, and "Shade: both" also stopped the bounce reading the frame. Each of those
rungs changed a second thing that its name did not mention, which is exactly what a rung exists
not to do.

What goes: candidates A, C and D in radianceFrom; B and E in the reflection pass, which never
runs now that its value is held at zero; F, the water plane from the primary hit; and the wider
probe of rungs 28 and 29. What changes: the water pass-through in both any hit shaders and the
translucent bit on a reclassified draw both read "rung 30 and up", which meant rung 30 and every
reflection candidate built on it. They now end at 33, the last live rung built on 30, so a rung
numbered 34 or later can differ from Off in only the thing it names. Rungs 27 to 29 keep their
classification, which is inert with the reflection pass standing down.

With the Experiment row at Off none of this runs, and with the ray tracing row Off none of the
shader runs at all.
---
